Changelog: 22-10-2026 19:31:16

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:09:08

Added. Pictures from SteamGridDB for the games in Steam (owner, 22-10-2026), with the suite's SteamGridDB API key
(core's covers), entered under the new Covers… button. A game brings no pictures, so all four were drawn from the app's
icon and the title; with the key, Update Game Mode first looks each ticked game up by its file name without the tags in
brackets ("(USA)", "(Disc 1)") and takes the cover, the wide picture, the banner and the logo with the highest score,
each in place of the drawn one; a picture SteamGridDB does not have stays drawn. What is found is kept in
~/.local/share/bc250-swanstation-manager/covers under the game's disc ID (SLUS-00594), or a name from its title without one, so a game is
asked for once; a game in Steam not yet looked up turns Update Game Mode on. A refused key or no network stops the
lookup with a message, and the shortcuts are written all the same. Without a key nothing changes. The artwork is now
drawn in the background job, after the lookup. install.sh --uninstall --purge removes the covers folder too; the installer test checks it. Test: the pictures from SteamGridDB in place of the drawn ones with a
No-Intro file name, and Covers… with Update Game Mode in the window, SteamGridDB's answers recorded.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 14:25:29

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 12:44:22

Added. SwanStation Manager: PS1 games on the BC-250 with the SwanStation core of RetroArch. The app installs RetroArch
from Flathub (a Flatpak, for the user, or uses the one that is installed) and the SwanStation core from the libretro
build server (checked as a zip with one x86-64 Linux library; the build server keeps only the newest build, so the core
is not pinned: the app records its build date and SHA-256, says when there is a newer build, also in the portal's notice
of updates outside the suite, and installs it on Update). It shows the PS1 BIOS in RetroArch's system folder (Open
folder, to copy yours in), finds the games in the chosen folders (CUE sheets with their BIN files, M3U playlists, CHD,
PBP and ISO, IMG or BIN images that are PS1 discs, with the disc ID from SYSTEM.CNF) and puts the ticked ones in Steam
for Game Mode, "[PS1] Title", the artwork drawn from the app's icon. The Game Mode shortcuts run
~/.local/bin/bc250-swanstation-run, which starts the RetroArch Flatpak with the core (--fullscreen) and, when Steam
starts a game on a Wayland desktop, without RetroArch's Wayland socket so Steam's overlay works. Not tried on the board
yet: the Flatpak install, a game from Game Mode, the controllers under Steam Input.
